    "body": "Hands-on check (macOS release build of e0219f1, contributor): import, 3D preview, tip pick, both refusals (+X axis, body below the tip), Apply body with the amber envelope, Cmd+Z / Cmd+Y, and the body drawn in the sim only when applied all behave as intended. Two follow-ups from that check are pushed:\n- 9656e4c / 11f522b: when a tool has a body, the sim also draws the cutter and shank (revolved from `Tool::profile`), so the holder sits on the tool instead of floating 55 mm above the axis marker. Tools without a body are unchanged. Frame's extent is left as before. Pinned by `the_simulated_tool_reaches_from_its_tip_into_the_body_on_the_users_document` (on the contributor's own test file) and `the_display_assembly_runs_from_the_tip_through_the_shank_into_the_body`.\n- 083762a: zoom (wheel or pinch, about the cursor, clamped 1/4x to 32x) and Fit (button or double-click) in the editor's 3D body preview. Pinned by `the_preview_zoom_clamps_and_fit_resets_it`.\n\nui lib: 309 pass. The only failures are `headless_run_succeeds` (no GPU here) and the release-lane `tool_editor_snapshot` (#359). Still a draft until the contributor re-checks zoom and the drawn tool.",
