    "body": "Hands-on check (contributor, macOS release build of add3a87):\n- Preview zoom, pinch, orbit and Fit work.\n- The sim draws the cutter, shank and holder cylinder for a tool without a body, and the cutter, shank and collar with one.\n- Cmd+Z swaps them back.\n\nadd3a87 itself: the sim always draws the running milling tool. That is the cutter and shank from `Tool::profile`, plus the body, or the parametric Ø holder_d × holder_len cylinder the collision laws judge. Lathe insert kinds keep the axis marker. Pinned by `the_simulation_draws_the_tool_with_its_holder_cylinder_or_its_body` and `without_a_body_the_display_is_the_profile_with_its_holder_cylinder`. Running the final quick gate.",
